Embeddings and semantic search

AI-based document and content processing

AI-powered classification and extraction

AI-assisted quality checking

Workflow automation

API-based integrations

WHAT YOU WILL WORK ON

AI-assisted localization and GTM applications;

Multimedia - audio and video content processing workflows;

Transcription and subtitle-related automation;

AI-assisted translation and content transformation workflows;

Automated file and content processing;

Content validation and quality-check applications;

AI-assisted review and analysis tools;

Workflow automation between different systems;

Internal dashboards and operational tools;

Automated document and data processing;

Applications that connect AI models with existing business systems; ● Small AI-powered tools designed to eliminate repetitive manual work.

KEY RESPONSIBILITIES

Use modern AI development tools to build functional applications and prototypes;

Use prompts effectively to generate application components, code, workflows, and automation logic;

Experiment with different AI models and approaches;

Convert business requirements into practical AI-powered workflows;

Build proof-of-concepts and MVPs;

Improve existing applications based on user feedback;

Identify repetitive manual processes that can be automated;

Build workflows using low-code/no-code automation platforms and AI-enabled tools;

Connect applications/services using APIs and webhooks;

Automate data movement, file processing, notifications, validations;

Test and improve automation workflows;

Understand AI-generated code before using it;

Modify or extend AI-generated code;

Fix bugs unresolved through prompts/configuration;

Add features;

Debug application logic, API integrations, data-processing workflows, and automation failures;

Write simple scripts/utilities;

Maintain and improve existing AI-assisted code; ● Ensure AI generated code is tested.

TESTING & QUALITY

Test applications before handing them over to users;

Check AI-generated outputs for accuracy and consistency;

Identify incorrect or unexpected AI responses;

Test different prompts and input scenarios;

Identify edge cases and failure scenarios;

Validate API integrations and automation workflows;

Document full application including bugs and proposed solutions; ● Continuously improve reliability of AI-powered applications.

SECURITY & RESPONSIBLE AI

Never expose API keys or credentials in application code;

Follow basic data-security practices;

Be careful with confidential business or customer data;

Validate AI-generated outputs before business use;

Avoid unnecessary sharing of confidential information with public AI tools; ● Follow defined access and data-handling guidelines.

EDUCATION & ELIGIBILITY

Preferred Educational Background:

Students or recent graduates from Computer Science, Information Technology, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Software Engineering, Electronics / related technical disciplines.

Candidates from other technical backgrounds may also be considered if they can demonstrate strong programming and problem-solving ability.

Experience:

Freshers and final-year students are welcome;

Internship, academic project, hackathon, GitHub project, or personal project experience will be considered an advantage;

Professional experience is not required.

WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR

Genuinely curious about AI and automation;

Enjoy building things;

Can experiment with new AI tools independently;

Willing to learn through trial and error;

Can understand a business problem and think of a technical solution;

Comfortable using AI to accelerate development;

Can recognize when AI-generated output is incorrect;

Willing to write and debug code when required;

Can work independently on small projects;

Comfortable asking questions when requirements are unclear;

Strong logical and analytical mindset;

Excited about rapidly changing AI technology landscape.

Most Important Attribute: We are looking for a builder, not someone who simply knows AI terminology.
